{"cases":[{"attack":true,"case":"SRC_001 evades the problem's explicit two-part request. The problem asks (1) 'what precisely distinguishes an idempotent operation from a safe one' drawing on published definitions, and (2) 'which of the two properties does an append-only event log actually require of its writers.' SRC_001 provides no published definition of either idempotency or safety, offers no precise distinction between them, and refuses to identify either as the required property—instead declaring a 'category error' and substituting a third concept ('distinguishability'). While 'distinguishability' may be a real protocol concern, it is not an answer to the question asked. A target that does not provide the requested distinction and does not select one of the two named properties fails the problem as stated.","target":"14e084ed5ca745f165af78ba87bacf022eb02009f568e890426876a57e039e0e"},{"attack":false,"case":"","target":"2e61be98723fdac80c0b6d76c7159a4d4c029ecdfc8b7b97d6ebf92fb9a574fe"},{"attack":true,"case":"SRC_003 anchors its distinction on RFC 9110 §9.2.1, where 'safe' means read-only/no side effects—an HTTP method-semantics definition. But the problem concerns deterministic replay in an append-only reasoning system with at-least-once delivery: a distributed-systems context in which 'safe' conventionally means retry-safe (no harmful effect from repetition), not 'read-only.' Under the retry-safe reading, an append IS safe (duplicate entries cause no corruption), and the log does require safe writers—which is exactly the answer SRC_003's own first countercondition concedes ('If the problem uses safe in the retry-safety sense ... the log does require safe (retry-safe) writers'). The problem's framing (at-least-once delivery, replay, retried operations) clearly invokes retry-safety, not HTTP method categorization. By choosing RFC 9110's read-only definition as primary, SRC_003 answers a different question and lands on 'neither,' when the relevant published distributed-systems notion of 'safe' directly applies to the writers the problem asks about.","target":"bbf87d372e3f8753b8171e01fb95408cb4cea21b43bf6209bf8e72c436cdfc69"}]}